    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d899">

                <pb facs="0875" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg777"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Allen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 149.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches Nos. 241 and 242, of April 14 and 18 last, respectively, on the
                    subject of Japanese interference with the Seoul Electric Railway, which is held
                    by Americans as mortgagees.</p>
                <p>You report that you and the Japanese minister have arranged the matter to the
                    satisfaction of all the parties concerned, and that it was only by prompt action
                    that serious loss to the American firm and injury to American prestige were
                    prevented.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your action.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
